-- title:
--   Sixth-power word envelope for the prime-selection core
-- statement:
--   For natural input size $n$, use the scheduled dimensions $h=\operatorname{microHalf}(\operatorname{inputBits}(n))$ and $J=\operatorname{blockCount}(\operatorname{inputBits}(n))$. Let $S=\operatorname{scale}(n)$, the sum of the shared-bank magnitude envelope, local-cover initialization envelope, maximum modulus, prime window, $n$, and $100$.
--   Let $U$ be a natural input-magnitude parameter, $P=\operatorname{maxMod}(n)$, $R=\operatorname{radix}(n)$, $Y=\operatorname{primeWindow}(n)$, $g$ the scheduled band width, and $b=\operatorname{ColorBandBounds.count}(n,g)$ the owner-record bound. The prime core's numeric requirement satisfies
--   $$
--   \operatorname{PrimeCore.word}(P,n,n,n,g,b,R,Y,U)\le5000S^6+4U.
--   $$
--   This covers the depth-control computation, prime pool, and weighted band-score arithmetic used by the core. The bound is polynomial in the dimension scale and linear in the supplied value-magnitude parameter.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/EncodedColorPrimeResources.lean#L78-L116

